IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea-definitions`
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ea3-schedules`
IMPORT `ea3-claims`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore) -- ea3: TESTS FOR PART 15 (ss 115 to 126).
-- Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text cited beside the group, never copied from what the code printed.
-- Calendar facts the tests rely on (a calendar): 1 June 2025 and 4 January 2026 are Sundays; 15 June 2025 is a Sunday.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Fixtures
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`ea3 test no public holidays` MEANS LIST

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`ea3 test public holiday on 16 June 2025` MEANS LIST Date 16 6 2025

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 115(1A) (lines 4629-4636)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (a) a prescribed type of dispute; (b) a claim lodged before 1 April 2017.
#ASSERT `s 115(1A) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into or deciding the dispute` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(1A) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into or deciding the dispute` FALSE (JUST (Date 31 3 2017)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The day before 1 April 2017 is before it; 1 April 2017 itself is not "before 1 April 2017".
#ASSERT `s 115(1A) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into or deciding the dispute` FALSE (JUST (Date 1 4 2017)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Neither: not of a prescribed type and no claim lodged.
#ASSERT `s 115(1A) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into or deciding the dispute` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 115(2) and its proviso (lines 4640-4648)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The corresponding day: the same day of the month, and the last day of a shorter month (fork F3).
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the corresponding day one year before` (Date 15 6 2025) EQUALS Date 15 6 2024
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the corresponding day one year before` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 28 2 2023
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the corresponding day six months after` (Date 15 6 2025) EQUALS Date 15 12 2025
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the corresponding day six months after` (Date 31 8 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
-- The one-year rule, both sides of its end: a matter on the corresponding day is not "earlier than one year", the day before is.
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the one-year rule does not bar the matter counted from the event` (Date 15 6 2024) (Date 15 6 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the one-year rule does not bar the matter counted from the event` (Date 14 6 2024) (Date 15 6 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The last day for lodging within 6 months of the termination: 10 Dec 2025 (a Wednesday); a last day that is a Sunday moves to the next day that is not excluded (s 50(b) of the Interpretation Act).
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the last day for lodging a claim within 6 months of the termination` (Date 10 6 2025) `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 10 12 2025)
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the last day for lodging a claim within 6 months of the termination` (Date 4 7 2025) `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 5 1 2026)
-- No termination, a matter 1 Jun 2025 against a claim lodged 15 Jun 2025: one year before is 15 Jun 2024, so it is within the year.
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into the matter` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 15 6 2025) NOTHING FALSE `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A matter of 1 Jun 2024 against a claim lodged 15 Jun 2025 is earlier than 15 Jun 2024.
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into the matter` (Date 1 6 2024) (Date 15 6 2025) NOTHING FALSE `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A termination on 10 Jun 2025 and a claim lodged 20 Jun 2025 for a matter out of the termination: within 6 months, and within the year from either event.
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into the matter` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 20 6 2025) (JUST (Date 10 6 2025)) TRUE `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The proviso, both sides of its end (10 Dec 2025): lodged on that day it is within 6 months, the day after it is not.
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into the matter` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 10 12 2025) (JUST (Date 10 6 2025)) TRUE `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into the matter` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 11 12 2025) (JUST (Date 10 6 2025)) TRUE `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The proviso is about a matter out of the termination; a matter that is not, lodged late, is tested by the year only (fork F2).
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into the matter` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 11 12 2025) (JUST (Date 10 6 2025)) FALSE `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The text does not say which of the two events the year is counted from (fork F1): matter 15 Jun 2024, claim lodged 20 Jun 2025 (year back to 20 Jun 2024: barred), termination 10 Jun 2025 (year back to 10 Jun 2024: not barred).
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into the matter` (Date 15 6 2024) (Date 20 6 2025) (JUST (Date 10 6 2025)) FALSE `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A matter said to arise out of a termination, with no day of termination given.
#ASSERT `s 115(2) the Commissioner is not barred from inquiring into the matter` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 20 6 2025) NOTHING TRUE `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 115(1), (2A), (3), (3A), (3B), (3C), (4) (lines 4619-4692)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#ASSERT `s 115(1), (1A) and (2) the Commissioner may inquire into and decide the dispute` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Barred by (1A) or by (2): the text says "must not".
#ASSERT `s 115(1), (1A) and (2) the Commissioner may inquire into and decide the dispute` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(1), (1A) and (2) the Commissioner may inquire into and decide the dispute` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(1), (1A) and (2) the Commissioner may inquire into and decide the dispute` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A bar not answered.
#ASSERT `s 115(1), (1A) and (2) the Commissioner may inquire into and decide the dispute` TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 115(1), (1A) and (2) the Commissioner may inquire into and decide the dispute` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- A dispute not between those parties: the Act gives no power and does not say there is none (ruling (c)); a dispute arising out of neither source is outside the "where" and answers JUST FALSE (ruling (b)).
#ASSERT `s 115(1), (1A) and (2) the Commissioner may inquire into and decide the dispute` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- "where the dispute arises out of any term in the contract of service ... or out of any of the provisions of this Act" (ruling (b)): a dispute arising out of neither is outside the power. (re-read from the text on 2026-11-05; the expected value was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 115(1), (1A) and (2) the Commissioner may inquire into and decide the dispute` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(1), (1A) and (2) the Commissioner may inquire into and decide the dispute` FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Where a dispute fails both the parties and the "where" limb, the "where" limb is tested first and answers JUST FALSE (assumed, fork F28).
-- The order for payment, "pursuant to that decision" and "in the prescribed form".
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the Commissioner may order payment by the party of such sum as the Commissioner considers just` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the Commissioner may order payment by the party of such sum as the Commissioner considers just` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the Commissioner may order payment by the party of such sum as the Commissioner considers just` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The power to order payment is part of the power of s 115(1): where that power is not given, neither is the order. (re-read from the text on 2026-11-05; the expected value was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the Commissioner may order payment by the party of such sum as the Commissioner considers just` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(1) the Commissioner may order payment by the party of such sum as the Commissioner considers just` NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2A): a mediation by an approved mediator or a conciliation by a conciliation officer.
#ASSERT `s 115(2A) the Commissioner may direct the parties to attend the mediation or conciliation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(2A) the Commissioner may direct the parties to attend the mediation or conciliation` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(2A) the Commissioner may direct the parties to attend the mediation or conciliation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 115(2A) the Commissioner may direct the parties to attend the mediation or conciliation` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): the claim of a subcontractor for labour.
#ASSERT `s 115(3) the Commissioner may hear and decide the claim of the subcontractor for labour` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(3) the Commissioner may hear and decide the claim of the subcontractor for labour` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3A): $20,000 for an employee in a managerial or an executive position, both sides of the ceiling; no limit for others.
#ASSERT `s 115(3A) the order for the payment of money is within the limit` TRUE 20000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(3A) the order for the payment of money is within the limit` TRUE 20001 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(3A) the order for the payment of money is within the limit` FALSE 50000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(3A) the greatest sum the order for payment may be for` TRUE EQUALS JUST 20000
#ASSERT `s 115(3A) the greatest sum the order for payment may be for` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3C): 14 days after the date of the order.  Order on Monday 2 June 2025: the 14th day is Monday 16 June.
#ASSERT `s 115(3C) the application is made no later than 14 days after the date of the order` (Date 2 6 2025) (Date 16 6 2025) `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(3C) the application is made no later than 14 days after the date of the order` (Date 2 6 2025) (Date 17 6 2025) `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Order on Sunday 1 June: the 14th day is Sunday 15 June, an excluded day, so the period includes Monday 16 June (s 50(b) of the Interpretation Act)
#ASSERT `s 115(3C) the application is made no later than 14 days after the date of the order` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 16 6 2025) `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(3C) the application is made no later than 14 days after the date of the order` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 17 6 2025) `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- ... and if Monday 16 June is a public holiday, Tuesday 17 June.
#ASSERT `s 115(3C) the application is made no later than 14 days after the date of the order` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 17 6 2025) `ea3 test public holiday on 16 June 2025` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(3C) the application is made no later than 14 days after the date of the order` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 18 6 2025) `ea3 test public holiday on 16 June 2025` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The last day itself: 14 days after Monday 2 June is Monday 16 June; after Sunday 1 June, Sunday 15 June is excluded, so Monday 16 June; with Monday 16 June a public holiday, Tuesday 17 June.
#ASSERT `s 115(3C) the last day for making the application` (Date 2 6 2025) `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 16 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 115(3C) the last day for making the application` (Date 1 6 2025) `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 16 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 115(3C) the last day for making the application` (Date 1 6 2025) `ea3 test public holiday on 16 June 2025` EQUALS JUST (Date 17 6 2025)
-- (3B): an order made in the absence of a party, on that party's application, subject to (3C).
#ASSERT `s 115(3B) and (3C) the Commissioner may set aside or vary the order on the application` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(3B) and (3C) the Commissioner may set aside or vary the order on the application` TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(3B) and (3C) the Commissioner may set aside or vary the order on the application` TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 115(3B) and (3C) the Commissioner may set aside or vary the order on the application` FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 115(3B) and (3C) the Commissioner may set aside or vary the order on the application` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): "employer" includes the transferor and the transferee.
#ASSERT `s 115(4) "employer" the person is one` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(4) "employer" the person is one` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 115(4) "employer" the person is one` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 115(4) "employer" the person is one` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 116 (lines 4696-4735)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Arguments: an order under section 115 against an employer or person liable; the sum is payable to a workman or subcontractor for labour; after inquiry a contract is found.
-- "Whenever the Commissioner has made an order under section 115 ... to any workman or subcontractor for labour and after inquiry finds ... a contract" (ruling (b), 2026-11-05: "whenever" counts as "where").
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the Commissioner may order the other person to pay the money to the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the Commissioner may order the other person to pay the money to the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the Commissioner may order the other person to pay the money to the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The sum is payable to an employee who is not a workman: outside "any workman or subcontractor for labour" (read as the text's own no, fork F28).
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the Commissioner may order the other person to pay the money to the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not exceeding the amount found due: 500 found due and 300 admitted, so 300; 200 found due and 300 admitted, so 200.
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the greatest sum the order may require the other person to pay to the Commissioner` 500 300 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 116(1) the greatest sum the order may require the other person to pay to the Commissioner` 200 300 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 116(2) the other person need not be summoned before the Commissioner` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Where that other person admits to the Commissioner in writing" (ruling (b)): an oral admission gives no relief from summoning; JUST FALSE here is not "must be summoned". (re-read from the text on 2026-11-05; the expected value was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 116(2) the other person need not be summoned before the Commissioner` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3): liable as a principal under s 65 and the money admitted (600) is less than the salary (1,000): nothing relieves that person.
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the other person is relieved of liability for the balance of the salary` (JUST TRUE) 1000 600 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The money admitted (1,000) is sufficient: the subsection does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the other person is relieved of liability for the balance of the salary` (JUST TRUE) 1000 1000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the other person is relieved of liability for the balance of the salary` (JUST FALSE) 1000 600 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the other person is relieved of liability for the balance of the salary` NOTHING 1000 600 EQUALS NOTHING
-- The balance: 1,000 - 600 = 400, up to the amount for which the person is liable under s 65 (300 or 500).
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the balance of the salary for which the other person remains liable` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 300) 1000 600 EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the balance of the salary for which the other person remains liable` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 500) 1000 600 EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the balance of the salary for which the other person remains liable` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING 1000 600 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the balance of the salary for which the other person remains liable` (JUST TRUE) (JUST 300) 1000 1000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 116(3) the balance of the salary for which the other person remains liable` (JUST FALSE) (JUST 300) 1000 600 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 116(4) the person summoned is legally bound to attend at the time and place mentioned in the summons` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 116(4) the person summoned is legally bound to attend at the time and place mentioned in the summons` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 116(4) the person summoned is legally bound to answer the question truthfully` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 116(4) the person summoned is legally bound to answer the question truthfully` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 116(4) the person summoned is legally bound to answer the question truthfully` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): a discharge up to the amount paid of the money due.
#ASSERT `s 116(5) the amount of the money due under the contract that the payment discharges` 300 500 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 116(5) the amount of the money due under the contract that the payment discharges` 500 300 EQUALS 300

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 117 and s 118 (lines 4739-4771)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- 14 days after a decision on Monday 2 June 2025: Monday 16 June.
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the appeal is made within 14 days after the decision or order` (Date 2 6 2025) (Date 16 6 2025) `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An appeal on 17 June is outside the 14 days the text fixes in its own words (ruling (a), 2026-11-05, which overrules fork F7).
-- "within 14 days after the decision or order" (ruling (a); fork F7 overruled): 17 June is the 15th day. (re-read from the text on 2026-11-05; the expected value was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the appeal is made within 14 days after the decision or order` (Date 2 6 2025) (Date 17 6 2025) `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A decision on Sunday 1 June: the 14th day, Sunday 15 June, is excluded, so Monday 16 June is in time.
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the appeal is made within 14 days after the decision or order` (Date 1 6 2025) (Date 16 6 2025) `ea3 test no public holidays` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the person may appeal to the General Division of the High Court` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the person may appeal to the General Division of the High Court` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "Where any person interested is dissatisfied with the decision or order" (ruling (b)). (re-read from the text on 2026-11-05; the expected value was NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the person may appeal to the General Division of the High Court` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 117(2) the procedure governing the appeal is as provided for in the Rules of Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 117(2) the procedure governing the appeal is as provided for in the Rules of Court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The court to which the appeal lies is the General Division of the High Court, where the right to appeal is given.
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the court to which the appeal lies` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST `Body: the General Division of the High Court`
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the court to which the appeal lies` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 117(1) the court to which the appeal lies` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 118(1): no fee other than the registration fee.
#ASSERT `s 118(1) the Commissioner may charge the fee` `s 118(1) the registration fee at the rate in the Second Schedule` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 118(1) the Commissioner may charge the fee` `s 118(1) a fee of any other kind` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 118(1) the order made by the Commissioner is enforced by a District Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 118(1) the order made by the Commissioner is enforced by a District Court` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 118(2): a sale of immovable property only by the General Division of the High Court.
#ASSERT `s 118(2) the body may order a sale of immovable property for the purposes of the enforcement` `Body: the General Division of the High Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 118(2) the body may order a sale of immovable property for the purposes of the enforcement` `Body: a District Court` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 118(2) the body may order a sale of immovable property for the purposes of the enforcement` `Official: the Commissioner for Labour` EQUALS JUST FALSE

